From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: bound IPQ5332 host TX to completing rings

BE6500 IPQ5332 native group frames submitted on logical TCL ring 3 remain
pending while the first three rings release them. Ordinary 2.4 GHz TCP
also exhibits multi-second completion pauses on that ring and a CPU3
controlled transfer times out. Bypass the unreliable fourth host ring
on IPQ5332; keep QCN9274 and IPQ5424 ring counts unchanged.

Limit AHB completion IRQ setup to allocated TX rings and guard the
service routine against platform ring masks containing an unallocated
TX ring. RX/error/refill groups continue to operate. This is a bounded
host-path workaround; it does not establish the underlying firmware or
hardware mapping defect, nor change device-tree or user configuration.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp.c
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@ static int ath12k_wifi7_dp_service_srng(
 
 	if (dp->hw_params->ring_mask->tx[grp_id]) {
 		i = fls(dp->hw_params->ring_mask->tx[grp_id]) - 1;
-		ath12k_wifi7_dp_tx_completion_handler(dp, i);
+		if (i < dp->hw_params->max_tx_ring)
+			ath12k_wifi7_dp_tx_completion_handler(dp, i);
 	}
 
 	if (dp->hw_params->ring_mask->rx_err[grp_id]) {
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -679,7 +679,7 @@ static const struct ath12k_hw_params ath
 		.supports_shadow_regs = false,
 
 		.num_tcl_banks = 48,
-		.max_tx_ring = 4,
+		.max_tx_ring = 3,
 
 		.wmi_init = &ath12k_wifi7_wmi_init_qcn9274,
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -685,7 +685,7 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_config_ext_irq(str
 		/* TX masks use logical TCL ring indices.  WBM ring numbers are
 		 * hardware mappings and are not necessarily contiguous.
 		 */
-		for (j = 0; j < DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX; j++) {
+		for (j = 0; j < ab->hw_params->max_tx_ring; j++) {
 			if (ring_mask->tx[i] & BIT(j) &&
 			    num_irq < ATH12K_EXT_IRQ_NUM_MAX) {
 				irq_grp->irqs[num_irq++] =
